  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Xenon undergo $s p^3$ hybridization.\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/i0ZNfT3B-YuhX3bA91aJgh4M2fQM_l7FkSdy7tgoXb4.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nIn the fourth excited state xenon atom, has 8 unpaired electrons<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/6gNu5RP678q4GgSybrNVDgt8eCZoPHn9kmnfptruKBg.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nOne $s$ and three $p$ orbital undergo $s p^3$ hybridization. Four $s p^3$ hybrid orbitals form four $\\sigma$ bonds with oxygen atoms. They are $\\sigma s p^3-p$. Four $p \\pi-d \\pi$ bonds are also formed with oxygen atoms by the unpaired electrons.",
    "image": null
  },
